   "yaml": "id: BUG-041\ntitle: Create invoice with null or incomplete payment_details returns 500 instead of 422\nstatus: open\nseverity: major\nlayer: api\narea: invoices\naffects:\n  - POST /invoices\n  - POST /invoices/guest\nfound: 2026-10-11\nref:\n  - docs/api/contracts/Invoices_API.md#8-create-invoice\n  - docs/api/contracts/Invoices_API.md#9-create-guest-invoice\ndescription: >-\n  payment_details is only required to be present; only gift-card details have validation rules. null fails in the\n  controller (Arr::except and handlePayment(array $details)) with a PHP type error, answered as 500 \"Server Error\".\n  For the other methods the details go straight into the method's table: a missing NOT NULL column (bank_name,\n  account_name, account_number for bank-transfer) is MySQL error 1364 with SQLSTATE HY000, and app/Exceptions/Handler.php\n  checks HY000 before the error code, so it answers 500 \"Something went wrong\" (its 1364 -> 404 branch is never reached);\n  an unknown key or a too long value gives 500 too. The invoice row exists by then (BUG-040).\nsteps:\n  - Register a customer and log in.\n  - Send POST /carts with an empty body and take the returned id as the cart's id.\n  - Send POST /invoices with the customer's token, payment_method \"bank-transfer\", payment_details null, billing_street \"Stephansplatz 1\", billing_city \"Wien\", billing_country \"AT\" and the cart's id as cart_id.\n  - Send the same POST /invoices with payment_details {}.\n  - Send POST /invoices/guest without an Authorization header, with payment_method \"bank-transfer\", payment_details null, the same billing fields, the cart's id as cart_id, a unique guest_email, a guest_first_name and a guest_last_name.\nexpected: \"422 naming payment_details (or its missing bank_name, account_name and account_number) for each request, and no invoice created.\"\nactual: >-\n  500 for each request: { message: \"Server Error\" } for null on both endpoints, and { message: \"Something went wrong\" }\n  for {} on both endpoints (reproduced live on 2026-10-14: API-0500, API-0508, API-0501; on 2026-10-15: API-0670 for\n  {} on POST /invoices/guest, and API-0668 for null on POST /invoices again).\nevidence: |-\n  2026-10-14 18:54 UTC, throwaway customers (token ***), an empty cart from POST /carts for each request,\n  billing_street \"Stephansplatz 1\", billing_city \"Wien\", billing_country \"AT\":\n  POST /invoices { payment_method: \"bank-transfer\", payment_details: null, ... } -> 500 { message: \"Server Error\" } (API-0500)\n  POST /invoices { payment_method: \"bank-transfer\", payment_details: {}, ... } -> 500 { message: \"Something went wrong\" } (API-0501)\n  POST /invoices/guest { payment_method: \"bank-transfer\", payment_details: null, guest fields, ... }\n    -> 500 { message: \"Server Error\" } (API-0508)\n  2026-10-15 17:38 UTC, API-0670 (tests/api/invoices/post-invoices-guest.spec.ts, repeated x3, same result), no token,\n  Accept: application/json, an empty cart from POST /carts, the same billing fields, guest fields (email ***):\n  POST /invoices/guest { payment_method: \"bank-transfer\", payment_details: {}, ... } -> 500 { message: \"Something went wrong\" }\n  2026-10-15 ~17:37 UTC, API-0668 (repeated x3): POST /invoices { payment_method: \"bank-transfer\", payment_details: null, ... }\n    -> 500 { message: \"Server Error\" }; the invoice row was left behind (BUG-040).\n  Source (sprint5/API, c6032ad): StoreInvoice and InvoiceController::storeGuest (\"payment_details\" => ['present']);\n  InvoiceController::store and storeGuest (Arr::except on payment_details); Handler.php (HY000 checked before 1364);\n  migration payment_bank_transfer_details (bank_name, account_name, account_number NOT NULL).",
